hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20596","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard 'Ali ibn Zayd narrating from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from a man of his people called Malik, or Ibn Malik, narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Any Muslim who takes an orphan among two Muslim parents to his food and drink until he is independent, Paradise becomes obligatory for him outright; and any Muslim who frees a neck, or a Muslim man, it will be his ransom from the Fire; and whoever reaches his parents or one of them and enters the Fire, may Allah distance him."
"20597","Hushaym said: 'Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Malik ibn al-Harith, a man among them, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever takes an orphan among two Muslim parents to his food and drink until he is independent of him, Paradise becomes obligatory for him outright; and whoever frees a Muslim person, it will be his ransom from the Fire, recompensed limb for limb of him."
